        "end": {
          "line": 72,
          "character": 70
        }
      },
      "title": "The smaller shapes",
      "description": "**What it is:** the typed pieces inside the state.\n\n**How it works:**\n- `UserContext`: who you are, plus your loaded accounts, apps, ad units and connected networks.\n- `RoutingResult`: the router's decision: service, capability, reasoning and *path* (`reactive` for simple questions, `workflow` for complex ones).\n- `ToolCall`: one tool request: name, args, result, whether it's dangerous, and its approval status.\n\n**Why it matters:** read these and you know what every node can see.\n\n**Watch out:** `TypedDict` is only a type hint. Python doesn't check it at runtime."
    },
    {
      "file": "backend/chat/graph/state.py",
      "line": 164,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 161,
          "character": 1
        },
