          "line": 164,
          "character": 82
        }
      },
      "title": "Going backwards (in theory)",
      "description": "**How it works:** the graph has two arrows that go backwards: to the router when `needs_reroute` is set (a topic change, like *now show my Ad Manager orders*), and to the entity loader when `needs_entity_refresh` is set (after creating an app or ad unit). The router and entity loader clear these flags after they run.\n\n**Why it matters:** the design lets the graph loop back when the situation changes mid-answer.\n\n**Watch out:** nothing in the current code ever **sets** these flags, so the backward arrows are never taken. It's planned behaviour, not working behaviour. If asked, say it's wired into the graph but not triggered yet. Separately, there's a hard limit of 25 steps (later in this tour)."
    },
    {
