      },
      "title": "Seeing the graph",
      "description": "**What it is:** a tiny file for LangGraph Studio, a visual tool that draws your graph and lets you run it step by step.\n\n**How it works:** `backend/langgraph.json` points Studio at `studio.py:graph`. Run `langgraph dev` in `backend` to open it.\n\n**Why it matters:** seeing the boxes and arrows is the fastest way to understand this tour.\n\n**Watch out:** Studio uses its own in-memory storage, not your Postgres checkpointer."
    },
    {
      "title": "What you can do now",
      "description": "### What you can do now\n\n- Explain state, reducers, nodes and conditional edges using your own graph.\n- Say why queues go in the config and not the state.\n- Explain how the checkpointer makes pause and resume possible.\n- Name the per-message costs (rebuild, setup, new connection) and the 25-step limit.\n\n**Next:** *08 - Router and entity loader*. The first two nodes in detail."
    }
